FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the FerrionOS patches before it in recipe.toml applied, ferrion-drm-page-flip.patch last among them. It joins the submission requests of ferrion-gpu-submit.patch to the sync files of ferrion-gpu-syncobj.patch:
- sys_ioctl/redox/drm.rs: an EXECBUFFER with VIRTGPU_EXECBUF_FENCE_FD_IN names its sync file as the second descriptor of the call, so the driver receives the sync file itself; a negative descriptor gets EINVAL, as does one that is not a descriptor of the same scheme.
- redox-ioctl: FENCE_DUP_UNSIGNALED, the test-only command that made a fence no submission signals, is gone.

